      "writtenOn": "2024-01-15T09:25:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I was just thinking of situation:\n1) We receive MAX_QUEUED_REQUESTS at close time;\n \u003d\u003e Sent MAX_QUEUED_REQUESTS CMD_SEND_MAYBE_ENQUEUE_NETWORK_REQUEST_STATE_METRIC messages;\n \u003d\u003e Sent one CMD_SEND_PENDING_NETWORK_REQUEST_STATE_METRIC message;\n2) During the execution of CMD_SEND_PENDING_NETWORK_REQUEST_STATE_METRIC something happened before a message is popped mPendingState;\n3) Not sure whether it can happen: execution of the thread is not stopped due to some throttling and main thread execution is not stopped, but mPendingState is full;\n4) Result: we\u0027ll always skip all network request without any chance to empty the mPendingState queue.",
